@1 = ~Divine Soul~

@2 = ~Divine Soul: Divine souls, much like sorcerers, drew their powers from their innate connection to the divine, be it the direct touch of a god, a prophecy, or a celestial ancestor.

Advantages:

– May learn and cast cleric spells.
– May specialize in all weapons a shaman can use
– May specialize in all weapon styles and achieve mastery in dual–wielding.
– May turn undead as a cleric of the same level when channeling.

Disadvantages:
– May not learn and use any shaman–specific spells and abilities.
– May not learn and cast druidic spells.
– May not detect illusions.
– May not summon spirits when channeling.~

@3 = ~Druid~

@4 = ~Shaman~

@5 = ~Channel~

@6 = ~Channeling~

@7 = ~Stopped Channeling~